<title>USA: Greenspan wants end to special interest subsidies.</title>
<headline>Greenspan wants end to special interest subsidies.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan on Tuesday supported doing away with special-interest subsidies provided by the government.</p>
<p>&quot;I surely support removing subsidies which do not clearly create general welfare as distinct welfare of specific groups,&quot; he told the House Banking Committee.</p>
<p>His comments delighted Committee Chairman John Kasich, the Ohio Republican who is leading a fight in Congress against so-called corporate welfare.</p>
</text>
